From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:28:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/25] fill dl-a: polyTimeComputable_expSampleRaw reads the
 orbit polynomial by simp only

`rw [PolyExpr.eval_const]` rewrote only the first constant, leaving `(const 4).eval`
to close by defeq; the rule-10 seal (PolyExpr.eval irreducible) caught it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PqpVTiuDcjSqhyfbqnsVxA
---
 TCSlib/Cryptography/Candidates/DiscreteLog.lean | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/TCSlib/Cryptography/Candidates/DiscreteLog.lean b/TCSlib/Cryptography/Candidates/DiscreteLog.lean
index 0fdc5f19..e59792dc 100644
--- a/TCSlib/Cryptography/Candidates/DiscreteLog.lean
+++ b/TCSlib/Cryptography/Candidates/DiscreteLog.lean
@@ -924,7 +924,7 @@ theorem polyTimeComputable_expSampleRaw (H : ArithmeticFP) : PolyTimeComputable
   -- the trial loop (the repetition lemma, `n` rounds suffice: `R = var`)
   have hF := polyTimeComputable_iterateFind dla_ssStep_poly (dla_ssAcc_poly H) dla_ssOut_poly
     PolyExpr.var (PolyExpr.add (.mul (.const 2) .var) (.const 4)) (fun x i _ => by
-      rw [PolyExpr.eval_add, PolyExpr.eval_mul, PolyExpr.eval_const, PolyExpr.eval_var]
+      simp only [PolyExpr.eval_add, PolyExpr.eval_mul, PolyExpr.eval_const, PolyExpr.eval_var]
       exact dla_length_ssStep_iterate_le x i)
   -- the accepted block (marker dropped), `[]` on failure
   have hb := polyTimeComputable_tail.comp (hF.comp (dla_ssStart_poly H))
